  "notes": "USAGE:\n{憶測|おくそく} generally has a negative connotation, implying that the conclusion drawn is not well-founded. It is common in news commentary and formal discussions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {憶測|おくそく}が{飛|と}び{交|か}う (speculation flies around)\n- {憶測|おくそく}で{判断|はんだん}する (to judge based on speculation)\n- {憶測|おくそく}に{過|す}ぎない (it's nothing more than speculation)\n- {憶測|おくそく}を{呼|よ}ぶ (to invite speculation)\n- {憶測|おくそく}{記事|きじ} (speculative article)\n\nWRITING:\nAlso written as {臆測|おくそく} with a different first character. Both writings are accepted and have the same meaning.",
